// Explicit unit type `()` in type position (SPEC 3.5, FEATURES TYPE-05).
//
// Status: parses and passes `cell check`. `-> ()` is the same unit as an
// omitted `->`, lowered to C `void` (and to a void function in LLVM/MLIR).
// Unit values are not first-class: a `let` of `()`, a parameter of `()`, or
// a struct field of `()` is refused. Tuples are not implemented; anything
// inside the parens is a parse error.

pub fn nothing() -> () {
    return
}
